Here's a simple, beginner-friendly game structure:

```
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    int num1, num2;
    printf("Enter first number: ");
    scanf("%d", &num1);
    printf("Enter second number: ");
    scanf("%d", &num2);

    if (num1 > num2) {
        printf("Too small!\n");
    } else if (num1 < num2) {
        printf("Too small!\n");
    } else {
        printf("Both are equal!\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This uses `scanf` for input, `printf` for output, and `if` for conditional logic. For a more complex game, you'd add variables, loops, and error handling.
